# Vue client

- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` and Pinia. Keep connection state in a store, not in scattered component refs.
- Views render. Stores call `client/src/api`. The API client calls this app's `/api/v1` only.
- The token field exists only on the entry form. After a successful session response, drop it from component state. Do not put it in Pinia, `localStorage`, or `sessionStorage`.
- Screens: token entry, then connection (status, connect, QR or pairing code, reconnect, disconnect). No create, delete, or logout controls.
- Poll status and QR through our API while a connection attempt is in progress. Stop polling when the view unmounts or the session ends.
- Style with Tailwind utilities. Match existing spacing and color choices in the screen you are editing.
- Router guards send unauthenticated users to the token screen. Treat `401` from our API as a signed-out session.
